EmailTemplate.textOnly:
Hello {!Contact.FirstName},

The Transfer Achievement Award is for eligible residents; however, it is based upon both high academic achievement (3.5+ cumulative GPA) and financial need. Typically, a good indicator of financial need is if you are eligible to receive the Pell Grant, which would automatically be listed with your financial aid awards on your My ASU account once you are admitted to ASU and your FAFSA has been reviewed.

ASU is recognized as a top school in the nation for value so you can feel confident in knowing that the investment you are making in your education will pay off. Still, I understand that university tuition can be intimidating. I encourage you to explore additional scholarships that are offered to transfer students -- see the links below:

scholarships.asu.edu/transfers

scholarships.asu.edu/colleges

students.asu.edu/scholarships/resources

You may also be interested in searching for student jobs: students.asu.edu/financialaid/jobs

Please feel free to contact me if you have additional questions. I am happy to help.

{!User.Recruiter_Full_Name__c}
Admission Services
{!User.Recruiter_Title__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Email__c}
{!User.Recruiter_Phone__c}

If you have any additional information or questions related to this, please reply to this email.

{!Case.Thread_Id}
